{"id": "sevt_012yLkw3yeQATWza6CeV992J", "content": [{"text": "**Finding: the checkout deploy `a3f9c21` introduced an N+1 query pattern, and p99 latency jumped as soon as it went live.**\n\n**Evidence**\n\n- **Deploys:** `a3f9c21` (alice, \"refactor order summary builder for readability\") shipped to checkout at 14:31:18Z. Other deploys in the 6h window are cart at 09:14, auth at 11:02 and inventory at 14:55. Only checkout's deploy sits right before the spike, and inventory's 14:55 deploy comes 23 minutes after p99 had already risen.\n- **Latency:** checkout p99 was 56\u201377 ms through 14:31. It was 347 ms at 14:32, 852 ms at 14:33, and 1,488 ms by 14:35. It peaked near 3.6 s at 14:40 and was still 2\u20133.5 s at 15:00. The gap from deploy to first movement is about one minute.\n- **Diff:** the old code ran one batched query, `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id__in=order_ids)`, then grouped items in memory. The new code runs `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=order.id)` inside a loop, so each open order costs one database round trip.\n- **Log:** the `order_items` per-order query first appears at 14:31:18.144Z, the same second as the deploy. From then on, 1,000\u20131,300 per-order queries run each minute. Across 2,586 requests that hit the path, the median is 12 queries per request and the maximum is 16. Each query takes about 13 ms, so the added latency comes from the query count per request.\n\n**Not explained by this deploy**\n\n- Checkout error rate went from about 0.1% to 0.1\u20130.2% starting at 14:40. Nothing in this data links it to the N+1 yet, so it is still open. I haven't checked `db_pool_utilization` or upstream dependencies.\n- The log has about 1,900 GC-pause warnings across services. They look like background noise and don't line up with the checkout spike.\n\n**Suggested next steps (not executed)**\n\n- Roll back `a3f9c21`, or restore the batched `order_id__in` query. That is the fastest way to recover p99.\n- Add a test or query-count assertion so a per-row query in this path fails CI.\n- Check `db_pool_utilization` for checkout to see whether the error rate is connection-pool pressure from the extra queries.\n\n**Root cause:** `a3f9c21` \u2014 the refactor replaced one batched `order_items` query with a per-order query inside a loop, so each checkout summary request issues about 12 extra round trips and p99 climbs from about 70 ms to multiple seconds.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T11:50:51.345565Z", "type": "agent.message"}
